# VFGNHS Library System conventions

## Stack and architecture

- Frontend: React 18, TypeScript, Vite, Tailwind 4, and Lucide icons.
- Backend: Spring Boot 3.5, Java 17, JPA/Flyway, Spring Security, and JWT.
- Keep public OPAC routes open; enforce STUDENT, TEACHER, and ADMIN permissions server-side.
- The backend database is the source of truth. Do not use frontend demo records as live data.
- Preserve compatibility with H2 development and MySQL production migrations.

## Responsive UI

- Every screen must work on mobile, tablet, laptop, and desktop.
- Build mobile behavior with the feature; do not postpone it to a separate pass.
- Avoid fixed-width layouts that force page-level horizontal scrolling.
- Wide data tables may use a clearly bounded horizontal scroller; forms and actions must stack or wrap.
- Keep touch targets at least 40px and retain keyboard-visible focus states.

## Data and security

- Never expose password hashes or existing passwords. Admins may only reset passwords.
- Validate permissions, uniqueness, and payloads in the backend, not only in the browser.
- Never commit production secrets or `.env`; use environment variables for credentials and JWT keys.
- Keep audit entries free of passwords, tokens, and other secrets.

## Print and quality

- Preserve the approved borrower-card and book-card layouts and A4 print dimensions.
- Hide application chrome when printing; verify print after global CSS changes.
- Run frontend typecheck, lint, tests, and build plus backend tests for relevant changes.
